      "id": 9019,
      "q": "In a hypothetical banking system, banks initially hold exactly their required reserves. The reserve ratio stays at 15%. Banks lend all excess reserves, every loan payment is fully redeposited, and there is no currency drain or other lending constraint. The public deposits $30 million in currency it previously held. Including this initial deposit, what is the maximum total increase in deposits?",
