      "feedback": "The graph gives value of money 2 at a and 1.5 at b. Their reciprocal price levels are 1/2 and 2/3, a one-third increase. Proportional nominal wage growth leaves the real wage unchanged; nominal changes alone do not raise real productive capacity. With real output fixed, this graph requires velocity to fall to two-thirds of its initial value; it is not the fixed-velocity quantity-theory case.",
